{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO/JCO no-fault eviction relocation assistance","requirement":"Before evicting tenants from RSO- or JCO-covered units for a no-fault reason, a landlord must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD, serve the notice only afterward, and pay relocation assistance within 15 days of service.","key_value":"Eligible tenant $11,000 (<3 years) to $14,400 (3+ years); qualified tenant $23,150 to $27,400; per unit, July 1, 2026–June 30, 2027","coverage_conditions":"All residential rental units covered by the Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance or the Just Cause Ordinance; relocation assistance is paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"RSO- or JCO-covered rental units"},"exemptions":"Evicting a resident manager to replace another resident manager; eviction required by hazardous conditions from a natural disaster not caused by landlord negligence; landlord may offset accumulated rent against relocation assistance. Reduced amounts for Mom and Pop properties (four or fewer units) apply only to owner/relative/manager occupancy evictions.","penalty":"Failure to file the landlord declaration makes the eviction a violation of the RSO or JCO; tenant may raise non-payment as an affirmative defense and may pursue a private right of action.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":"Parallel JCO provisions at LAMC §§ 165.03 and 165.06; HCA state amounts must be paid where higher.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance demolition relocation","requirement":"An owner demolishing a Protected Unit for new construction must provide relocation under one of three RPO options, pay the highest of state and city amounts, and give tenants up to six months' notice plus return and first-refusal rights.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Protected Units demolished for the purpose of new construction, when demolition occurs within 5 years after filing the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Protected Units demolished for new construction"},"exemptions":"If the units to be demolished are not Protected Units or are not occupied by a lower income tenant, the regular RSO or JCO relocation rules apply instead.","penalty":"Failure to comply may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","effective_date":"2025-02-11","citation":"Ordinances #188481 and #188482 (Resident Protections Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Owners who demolish a Protected Unit for the purpose of new construction within 5 years after the filing of the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD are required to comply with relocation requirements under the RPO.","interaction":"Owner must pay the highest of applicable State (HCA) and City relocation amounts; RPO applies only to Protected Units.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Housing Crisis Act relocation for lower-income demolition displacees","requirement":"Under the Housing Crisis Act, relocation payments to lower-income tenants (80% AMI or lower) displaced by demolition for new construction must be enhanced above the RSO or JCO amounts, regardless of whether the City's RPO applies.","key_value":"80% AMI threshold; benefits under Gov. Code ch. 16 (commencing with § 7260)","coverage_conditions":"Lower income households (80% AMI or lower) displaced by demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Lower-income households displaced by demolition for new construction"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 66300.6","quoted_span":"The RSO and JCO amounts must also be enhanced for lower income tenants under the HCA regardless of the RPO applicability.","interaction":"Owner must pay the higher of HCA state amounts or City RSO/JCO amounts.","confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
